{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cosy-returnable-arachnid","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\nThe repository has **45 shell scripts** and no ShellCheck gate. A destructive\n`rm -rf \"${dir}\"/*` pattern — the shape that caused a real `rm -rf /*` incident on\na developer workstation on 2026-08-26 — is detected by ShellCheck **SC2115** but\nnothing in `make lint` runs it. Add ShellCheck to the lint gate and clear the\nexisting findings.\n\n## Why SC2115 specifically, and why warning severity\n\nVerified against the incident's exact line:\n\n```sh\ndir=\"$REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\"\nrm -rf \"${dir}\"/.[!.]* \"${dir}\"/*\n```\n```\nprobe.sh:3:24: warning: Use \"${var:?}\" to ensure this never expands to /* . [SC2115]\n```\n\nThe hardened form is clean:\n```sh\n: \"${dir:?empty}\"\n(cd -- \"${dir:?}\" && rm -rf -- ./*) || exit 1\n```\n\n**SC2115 is emitted at `warning`, not `error`.** A gate configured at\n`-S error` would NOT have caught this. The gate must run at `-S warning`.\n\n## Current findings (measured, shellcheck 0.11.0)\n\nScope: 45 `*.sh` files excluding `.venv/`, `.git/`, `.claude/`.\n\n- `-S error`: **1** finding\n- `-S warning`: **9** findings, confined to **2 files**\n\n| File | Findings |\n|---|---|\n| `infra/terraform/user_data.sh` | SC2154 (line 25), SC2034 (line 88), SC2066 error (line 104) |\n| `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` | SC1083 x6 (lines 75, 76, 80 — literal braces) |\n\nNone are the destructive-`rm` class; the 6 `rm -rf` sites on `main` all use the\nsafe quoted `rm -rf \"$tmp\"` form against `mktemp -d` results.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn scope: wiring ShellCheck into `make lint`, clearing the 9 findings, documenting\nthe dev-tool dependency.\n\nOut of scope: hardening `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` — that file does not\nexist on `main`; it lives only on the unmerged `fix-mcp-clone-blocks-boot` branch.\nOnce the gate exists, that branch's `rm -rf \"${dir}\"/.[!.]* \"${dir}\"/*` line\ncannot land without tripping SC2115, which is the point.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `make lint` runs ShellCheck at `-S warning` over every tracked `*.sh` file,\n   excluding vendored paths (`.venv/`, `.git/`, `.claude/`), and fails the build on\n   any finding.\n2. A file containing `rm -rf \"${dir}\"/*` fails `make lint` with SC2115; the\n   `: \"${dir:?}\"` + `cd -- \"$dir\" && rm -rf -- ./*` form passes. Covered by a test.\n3. The 9 existing findings are resolved — fixed where the code is genuinely wrong,\n   or suppressed with a targeted `# shellcheck disable=SCxxxx` carrying a one-line\n   justification comment. No blanket file-level or repo-level disables.\n4. `make lint` degrades with a clear, actionable message when ShellCheck is not\n   installed, naming the install command. It must not silently skip — a skipped\n   gate is indistinguishable from a passing one.\n5. Enforcement lives in `make lint` (which both the pre-commit hook and CI invoke),\n   not in a CI-provider-specific workflow step, satisfying `project.portability`.\n6. The ShellCheck dependency is documented in the dev-environment setup alongside\n   the existing ruff/mypy tooling.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- `make lint` green on a clean tree with ShellCheck wired in.\n- The AC-2 regression test passes and fails correctly when the guard is removed.\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md` names ShellCheck as a required dev tool.\n- No new complexity-baseline or module-size violations introduced.\n\n## Notes\n\nFiled from the 2026-08-26 workstation incident, where a mutation test removed a\nguard function from a script performing real filesystem deletion and then executed\nit unsandboxed. Research finding worth recording: **no mutation-testing tool in any\nlanguage isolates runtime side effects** — cargo-mutants, mutmut, Stryker, PIT and\nmull all isolate only the source tree, and cargo-mutants documents this hazard\nexplicitly at https://mutants.rs/cautions.html. ShellCheck is the cheapest control\nthat would have prevented the specific line from ever landing; sandboxing the\nmutation run is the broader fix and is tracked separately.","id":"fe4e-54a5-3c3a-4901","parent_id":"","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["infra","lint","safety"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add ShellCheck to the lint gate at warning severity to catch SC2115 rm -rf glob hazards"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787773559816020777,"uuid":"54bba6fa-1de3-4f6e-9eab-79c62ed1855e"}